{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_161184867#1_342518055","relevance":3,"reason":"This is another segment of the same Beliefnet article already seen, but it is still directly dedicated to religion in public schools and explains that academic teaching about religion, world religions requirements, curriculum standards, and limits on teacher-led prayer are allowed/important.","learned":"Repeated evidence: public schools may teach about religion academically, including world religions in social studies/geography standards, while teacher-led prayer is prohibited."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1585","reason":"Although one duplicate appeared, the query has already produced multiple grade-3 results; continue to see if more distinct legal/explanatory documents appear."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1585"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_00_744067170#4_1389605075","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1585","rank":4,"snippet":"likelihood of exclusivity and bullying diminishes. 3. Religious literacy is key to a well-rounded education. If students are to function as globally competent citizens, they need to understand religion’s profound impact on history, politics, society, and culture. They should know basic religious facts and principles and recognize the diversity that exists within each belief system across time and place. Familiarity with central religious texts is also important, and it’s <cover>legal to study these texts in public schools, as long as the purpose is educational and not personal or devotional. For example, the Bible can be studied as a piece of literature that has influenced many classic works. 4. Students have a First Amendment right to religious expression in school. The U.S. Constitution contains two clauses, known as the religion </cover>clauses, which inform the relationship between religion and public schools.\" , \"start_char\": 2703.000000 , \"title\": \"Four Reasons Why You Should Teach About Religion in School (Opinion)\" , \"url\": \"http://blogs.edweek.org/edweek/global_learning/2014/04/four_reasons_why_you_should_teach_about_religion_in_school.html\" }"}}
