{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1021154953#1_1833251160","relevance":3,"reason":"The article directly concerns religious expression in public schools and gives evidence that religion appears through student prayer and other student religious-expression rights, with public schools warned not to violate those rights.","learned":"Student prayer and religious expression are protected ways religion can appear in public schools, and schools may face federal consequences for infringing those rights."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1586","reason":"The current query is returning directly relevant results on concrete forms of religious expression in public schools, so continue through the list."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1586"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_40_1410993017#3_2892084679","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1586","rank":3,"snippet":"decision, some school administrators took things too far by prohibiting constitutionally protected student religious expression. Of course, other administrators and school boards practiced civil disobedience by continuing school-sponsored religious practices in defiance of the Court’s ruling. But in recent decades, most public school officials have begun to get religion — and prayer — right. They (finally) understand the difference between government speech promoting religion — which the establishment clause prohibits — and student religious speech, which the free-exercise and free-speech clauses protect. Visit most public schools today and you are likely to see students praying around the flagpole, attending religious club meetings, giving each other religious <cover>literature, saying grace before lunch, talking about their faith in class discussions and in other ways expressing their religious convictions. In fact, there is more student religious expression in public schools </cover>today than at any time since the 19th century.\" , \"start_char\": 1953.000000 , \"title\": \"50 years later, how school-prayer ruling changed America | Freedom Forum Institute\" , \"url\": \"https://www.freedomforuminstitute.org/2012/07/29/50-years-later-how-school-prayer-ruling-changed-america/\" }"}}
