{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_32_255626711#11_471663952","relevance":3,"reason":"This ACLU religious-freedom document is directly about religion in public schools and explains concrete ways it may appear, including individual student prayer, religious holidays, teacher-led prayer, graduation prayer, religious clubs, and Bible distribution, with limits on disruption and coercion.","learned":"Individual students may pray during the school day if they do not disrupt instruction or force others to join; public-school religion issues also include holiday celebrations, clubs, Bible distribution, and restrictions on school-official-led prayer."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1597","reason":"The religious-holidays query is yielding highly relevant ACLU guidance segments on multiple ways religion appears in public schools, so continue for more direct evidence."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1597"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_45_546680139#3_964628949","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1597","rank":3,"snippet":"own the school had a secular purpose for allowing the students to speak, and the process of selecting those speakers had nothing to do with what they would say. However, some courts have held that school officials may prevent students from delivering invocations as part of graduation ceremonies or giving commencement speeches that included Christian comments meant to convert their classmates. And the Supreme Court has held that a high school violated the establishment clause by arranging for students to give invocations over the public address system at football games, even though students created and led the prayers ( Santa Fe Independent School Dist. v. Doe, 530 U.S. 290 (2000)). School Celebrations of <cover>Religious Holidays Public schools need to be careful when they celebrate </cover>religious holidays. Schools may not put up explicitly religious symbols (like a nativity scene or menorah) unless they’re part of a larger holiday display that’s not religious.\" , \"start_char\": 2128.000000 , \"title\": \"Religion in Public Schools | Lawyers.com\" , \"url\": \"https://www.lawyers.com/legal-info/research/education-law/religious-beliefs-and-public-schools.html\" }"}}
