{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_1435369545#7_2962273838","relevance":3,"reason":"The OSPI guidance page is directly about religion in schools and explains how religion may appear in public schools through neutral facility access for religious organizations and through teaching about religion in public education, while rejecting devotional teaching of religion.","learned":"Public schools are not religion-free zones: they may teach about religion academically and may need to treat religious groups neutrally in facility-use requests, but may not teach religion as indoctrination."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1598","reason":"The religious-accommodations query has consistently produced grade-3 guidance segments on how religion appears in public schools, so continue while it remains productive and the judgment budget allows."}}
