{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_1639554712#8_3525009378","relevance":3,"reason":"The NCAC resource guide is explicitly dedicated to religious expression in public schools and directly explains how religion may appear through temporary religious symbols used as teaching aids, religious clothing and symbols as protected student expression, and curriculum issues involving evolution and creation science.","learned":"Public schools may display religious symbols temporarily as teaching aids in academic programs, and students' religious clothing or symbols are protected expression if not disruptive; schools may not shape science curriculum to promote religious doctrine."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1599","reason":"This resource-guide query is returning strong grade-3 evidence on religious expression in public schools, and there is still limited judgment budget to collect more direct results."}}
