{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_1639554712#5_3525003816","relevance":3,"reason":"The NCAC resource guide is explicitly dedicated to religious expression in public schools and directly explains how religion may appear or be limited through student-led prayer at football games and graduation, student-initiated prayer or personal messages, and the need to avoid school endorsement of religion.","learned":"Student-led or student-initiated prayer may arise at school events such as football games or graduation, but public schools must avoid circumstances that imply official endorsement of religion."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1599","reason":"The resource-guide query is producing strong grade-3 evidence on religious expression in public schools, and there is still budget to collect more direct results."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1599"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_1639554712#9_3525010947","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1599","rank":6,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_1639554712#9_3525010947\" , \"end_char\": 6002.000000 , \"headings\": \"The First Amendment in Schools: Resource Guide: Religious Expression in the Public Schools The <cover>First Amendment in Schools: Resource Guide: Religious Expression in the Public Schools\" , \"segment\": \"The Court rejected the state’s alleged secular purpose to protect academic freedom, finding it a “sham.” Religious Clothing and Symbols: </cover>Religious clothing and symbols, if not disruptive, are a protected form of expression. Even schools with dress codes ordinarily make an exception for religious articles. Released Time: Students may be dismissed from school for off-campus religious instruction, provided that the schools do not encourage or discourage participation or penalize those who do not attend. Zorach v. Clauson (1952). Use of Public School Facilities by Religious Groups: Under a 1993 Supreme Court ruling, public schools that permit their facilities to be used by community groups are not permitted to discriminate against religious groups. Lamb’s Chapel v. Center Moriches School District (1993).\" , \"start_char\": 5191.000000 , \""}}
