{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_1639554712#3_3525000638","relevance":3,"reason":"The NCAC resource guide is explicitly dedicated to religious expression in public schools and directly explains how religion may appear through academic teaching about religion, Bible use in history/civilization/ethics/comparative religion, discussion of religion's role in history and literature, and limits on school-sponsored prayer and Bible reading.","learned":"Public schools may teach about religion and use the Bible academically when serving secular educational goals, but they may not promote or inhibit religious belief or sponsor prayer and devotional Bible reading."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1599","reason":"The resource-guide query is still producing grade-3 evidence on concrete ways religion appears in public schools; use the remaining judgment budget on the next likely relevant result."}}
